tions. The bundled instructions must say that coverage artifacts under the `requirements.test-coverage.storage` location are disposable build output. That covers profiles, reports and captured source snapshots. They must also say these artifacts must not be staged or committed to Git.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_default_to_process_coverage_and_keep_artifacts_disposable]` carries the `{test}` reference and checks both.\n\n- **Home skill (`habeas`).** The test asserts the exact sentence \"are disposable build artifacts. Never stage or commit them to Git\". It asserts that the home skill contains \"Profiles, reports, and captured source\" and `target/habeas/coverage/`. The skill text I found has all of these in `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md`, section \"Testing and coverage artifacts\". The test also requires \"disposable\", \"Cargo target directory\" and a case-insensitive \"never stage or commit\" in each skill. That covers the storage location and the Git prohibition.\n- **Other two skills.** For `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, the test asserts \"never stage or commit disposable coverage artifacts in the Cargo target directory\". It also asserts the pointer to the habeas skill's \"Testing and coverage artifacts\" section. The searched skill text contains both.\n- **Assertion strength.** The checks are `contains` assertions on whitespace-collapsed skill text, with per-skill failure messages. A skill that omitted or reversed the guidance would fail them.\n\nThe test does not check `habeas-requirements` or `habeas-refactor`. The requirement does not say every bundled skill must repeat the guidance. The `habeas` home skill states it in full, and the two skills that handle coverage defer to it and repeat the prohibition. I treat that as adequate, so there is no testing gap.\n\nThe test also checks `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md` for the same guidance. That is extra evidence and not needed here.",
